Subject: DIET: meat

A funny thing happened to me recently.  I grew up eating beef or pork almost
every day.  In the past year or so I have largely dropped them from my diet
(unless milk counts).  Not out of any grand purpose; my habits and tastes
just changed according to what's available near where I work.  Lunch is
usually salmon maki; supper (if any) is typically a Vietnamese chicken dish.
 I eat about two hamburgers a month.

On December 18, I had a rare teriyaki steak for dinner.  The next day I had
diarrhoea and fever.  I infer that I've lost tolerance for the bacteria in
rare beef.  (I do not blame the restaurant; my ex and I often have sashimi
there, with no ill effect.)

I report this for whatever interest you may find in it.

On the question of meat cravings:  my ex says, "sometimes I crave meat, but
I find that what I'm really craving is salt; if I eat salt, the craving goes
away."

